{#
    One image out of the file manager — the `file` alias (ADR 0023).

    THE PLAIN TEXT FIELD STAYS THE FIELD, the same stance `search`, `rte` and `tabs` take. This
    fragment renders the file's id in an ordinary input and lets the module put a preview and a
    picker in front of it; what the browser submits is always this one input. Without the module
    an editor sees the id and can still paste one in — unlovely and working, where a field that
    needs JavaScript to be editable at all would be a step back from the display it replaces.

    THE PICKER DOES NOT NAVIGATE, and that is the requirement the story is built around: an
    editor who has to leave a half-filled form to pick an image loses the rest of it. The module
    fetches its entries from `field.pickerUrl` and never links there.

    THE CURRENT VALUE IS SHOWN AS AN ID AND NOT AS A NAME. Looking the name up would be one query
    per image field per form render; the preview image answers the same question better, and it
    costs the form nothing because the browser fetches it.

    `required` IS THE BROWSER'S MARKER AND NOT A SECOND VALIDATION. `#[Admin(required: true)]`
    marks the field; the authority on an empty value is the core, which answers a column that
    may not be null with a finding on this field (`FormController::payload()`). This package
    validates no field itself, and this one is no exception.
#}
{% include 'widget/_label.html.twig' %}
            <div class="admin-form__file" data-controller="admin-file-picker" data-admin-file-picker-url-value="{{ field.pickerUrl }}" data-admin-file-picker-field-value="field-{{ field.property }}" data-admin-file-picker-alias-value="{{ field.alias }}">
                <input class="admin-form__control" type="text" id="field-{{ field.property }}" name="{{ field.property }}" value="{{ field.value }}" data-admin-file-picker-target="source" autocomplete="off"{% if field.required %} required{% endif %}{% if field.error %} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>
                <p class="admin-form__hint" data-admin-file-picker-target="note">Ohne JavaScript steht hier die Id der Datei — sie lässt sich von Hand eintragen.</p>
            </div>
